c:
Because each hex digit is its own 4-bit group, the number of 1s in the binary form is the sum
of the 1-counts of the hex digits (the "1s" column of the hex table): 0 → 0; 1, 2, 4, 8 → 1;
3, 5, 6, 9, A, C → 2; 7, B, D, E → 3; F → 4.
